# FIXED 2026-10-11 (experiments/2026-10-11-libraries3/README.md); kept as the record of the bug.
# String#[] with a String argument (substring or nil) is Ruby's s["b"]; the cheat sheet lists
# String.[](x, Any, [Integer]), but the checker rejects a String index:
#   error: Indexable.[]: the index must be Integer, but is String [type]
# String.slice(s, "b") is accepted and works.
s = "abc"
p(s["b"])
p(String.[](s, "b"))
